  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 325.92pt, "Keywords: long-duration energy storage, heat electrification, energy system modelling, power-")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 344.876pt, "to-heat-to-power storage, lithium-ion battery.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(277.198pt, 375.832pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 406.788pt, "This study assesses the role of Power-to-Heat-to-Power Storage (PHPS) systems, also known as ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 425.744pt, "Carnot batteries, in the national energy system of a wind-dominated (Denmark) and a solar-")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 444.699pt, "dominated (Spain) region. Using the open-source PyPSA framework, we model sector-coupled ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 463.655pt, "electricity and heating systems, and evaluate individual and district heating configurations for ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 482.611pt, "heat provision at residential level, with and without PHPS waste heat recovery. Our results show ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 501.688pt, "that PHPS is most viable in individual heating systems, and in wind-dominated locations, where ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 520.644pt, "its low cost per energy capacity enables it to balance long-duration fluctuations. Moreover, waste ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 539.599pt, "heat recovery is essential to enhance PHPS competitiveness, allowing it to displace lithium-ion ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 558.555pt, "batteries. Conversely, PHPS is largely outcompeted in district heating systems, which favour low-")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 577.511pt, "cost centralized energy storage. Sensitivity analysis highlights that PHPS viability depends ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 596.466pt, "primarily on achieving low energy capacity costs (≤10 €/kWh) and maintaining reasonable heat-")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 615.422pt, "to-power conversion efficiencies. Overall, while PHPS complements existing storage ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 634.378pt, "technologies by providing dispatchable electricity and heat, its potential adoption is highly ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 653.333pt, "context-dependent, influenced by climate, heating system configuration, and competing storage ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 672.41pt, "costs. ")
]

