#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.84pt, 791.4pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 66.955pt, "European countries [33]. Both configurations are evaluated in two representative contexts: wind-")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 86.032pt, "dominated systems, characteristic of Northern Europe, and solar-dominated systems, ")
  #line-at(85.058pt, 104.988pt, "characteristic of Southern Europe.  ")
  #line-at(85.047pt, 135.944pt, "This article is divided into 7 main sections: after the introduction in section 1, the methodology ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 154.9pt, "and the modelled scenarios are described in Section 2. Results and Sensitivity Analysis are ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 173.856pt, "summarized in Sections 3 and 4, while Discussion is conducted in Section 5. The limitations of ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 192.811pt, "the study are included in Section 6. Finally, conclusions are gathered in Section 7. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 226.8pt, "2.")
  #line-at(103.079pt, 226.8pt, "Methodology ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 248.4pt, "The model developed using the open-source software PyPSA [34], simulates the operation of a ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 267.477pt, "single European country energy system of a full year with hourly resolution under perfect ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 286.433pt, "foresight. The system incorporates both power and heating sectors, each composed of various ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 305.388pt, "elements such as generators, demand loads and energy storage units. The capacities of these ")
  #line-at(85.047pt, 324.344pt, "components (e.g., generators or energy storages) and their dispatch are jointly optimized to meet ")
  #line-at(85.047pt, 343.3pt, "the demands, while minimizing the annualized total system cost. A key constraint in the ")
  #line-at(85.058pt, 362.256pt, "optimization is the limitation of CO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(245.04pt, 363.24pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.52pt, 362.28pt, " emissions to 5% of the 1990 values for each country. The ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 381.236pt, "model’s behaviour is governed by a set of equations and constraints, which are detailed in ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 400.191pt, "Appendix A. Additional information on PyPSA modelling tool, and its applications can be found ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 419.147pt, "in studies, such as [4], [35], [36], [37]. ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 450.225pt, "In this study we have compared two locations with different climate conditions in Europe. The ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 469.18pt, "wind-dominated location, represented by Denmark, is characterized by having high wind-")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 488.136pt, "generation and high heating demand. Conversely, the solar-dominated location, exemplified by ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 507.092pt, "Spain, has higher solar generation, and reduced heating demand. The data used for the simulations ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 526.047pt, "is plotted in Figure 1 and Figure B. 1 for Denmark and Spain, respectively. Panels a and b in ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 545.003pt, "Figure 1 depicts the hourly capacity factor (CF) data of solar and wind generation, respectively, ")
  #line-at(85.095pt, 563.959pt, "retrieved from [38], [39]. Panels c and d show the electricity and heating demand of the country ")
  #line-at(85.095pt, 582.914pt, "normalized to their respective average yearly demand from [40]. Wind generation in both climates ")
  #line-at(85.095pt, 601.87pt, "exhibits synoptic fluctuations, typically spanning a couple of days, with higher output during the ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 620.947pt, "winter months, correlating well with heating demand (panel d). As expected, solar generation in ")
  #line-at(85.084pt, 639.903pt, "both locations demonstrates daily variations. Each country is modelled as an isolated copperplate ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 658.859pt, "node, meaning that energy transmission between countries (exports or imports) and bottlenecks ")
  #line-at(85.073pt, 677.814pt, "within the country itself are neglected. ")
]

