  #line-at(85.08pt, 369.23pt, "Figure 2. Overview of the modelled energy system including the electrical bus with the generators ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 381.949pt, "and storages, and the heating bus with the thermal energy storages.  ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 404.625pt, "In addition to analysing the influence of the region on PHPS feasibility, we consider three ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 423.58pt, "configurations: (1) A base case, with neither CTES or ITES; (2) decentralized, representing PHPS ")
  #line-at(85.113pt, 442.536pt, "coupled with individual heating systems and including only ITES tanks; and (3) centralized, ")
  #line-at(85.113pt, 461.492pt, "representing PHPS integrated into a district heating system and including only the CTES tanks. ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 480.447pt, "Each configuration is evaluated under two use-case scenarios: “waste heat,” which includes waste ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 499.525pt, "heat utilization, and “no waste heat,” which excludes it, yielding a total of 12 combinations. ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 530.481pt, "A distinctive feature of PHPS is its simultaneous production of electricity and heat, with their ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 549.436pt, "ratio fixed by the H2P conversion efficiency, assumed constant at 0.3 in all simulations (Table 1). ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 568.392pt, "In the “waste heat” scenarios, this coupling means that PHPS discharge is constrained by the ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 587.348pt, "lower of the two demands: if no heat sink is available, either through immediate use or storage in ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 606.303pt, "CTES or ITES units, the system cannot be discharged, even when electricity demand exists. ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 637.26pt, "To facilitate the comparison between scenarios, we use the number of average hourly load (av.h.l) ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 656.215pt, "that can be covered with the optimized PHPS capacity. This value represents the hours of average ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 675.171pt, "power demand that could be covered by discharging the energy storage capacity. As a reference, ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 694.248pt, "the currently existing pumped hydro storage capacity in Spain is approximately 70 GWh [41], ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 713.204pt, "which considering and average power demand of 28 GW translates into to 2.5 av.h.l. When the ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 732.159pt, "optimal energy capacity for PHPS is below 2 av.h.l, PHPS is considered not contributing ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 751.115pt, "significantly to the energy system. It should be noted that this metric emphasizes the role of ")
]

