#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.08pt, 791.4pt, "15 ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 66.955pt, "configuration a more favourable option for balancing the system, and, consequently, leads to ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 86.032pt, "PHPS not being selected.  ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 116.989pt, "In a previous study, Victoria et al. [4] concluded that optimal solutions in Europe include both ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 135.944pt, "CTES and hydrogen to balance long-duration fluctuations of wind generation. This finding differs ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 154.9pt, "from our outcomes, where PHPS is not part of the optimal solution in wind-dominated regions ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 173.856pt, "when CTES is available provided waste heat is not utilized. This discrepancy can be attributed to ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 192.811pt, "the superior performance of hydrogen storage according to the techno-economic assumptions in ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 211.767pt, "[4], as it benefits from lower CPE, the absence of standing losses, and higher round-trip efficiency ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 230.723pt, "compared to PHPS.  ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 261.8pt, "PHPS is also selected in solar-dominated countries, particularly when waste heat is utilized. In ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 280.756pt, "such cases, PHPS can coexist with CTES, though its role becomes more prominent when paired ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 299.712pt, "with ITES systems. This configuration aligns with the prevalence of individual heating solutions, ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 318.667pt, "such as decentralized electric and gas boilers, common in these regions [33]. PHPS thus emerges ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 337.623pt, "as an optimal option for building-integrated applications producing both electricity and heat while ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 356.579pt, "storing waste heat in ITES. Large-scale buildings with substantial energy demands, such as hotels, ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 375.534pt, "sports centres, or industrial facilities that lack sufficient space for CTES, are well-positioned as ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 394.49pt, "early adopters, benefiting from the relatively large storage capacities and high energy density of ")
  #line-at(85.102pt, 413.446pt, "PHPS units [15]. Alternatively, PHPS could be deployed at a large scale in solar-dominated ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 432.523pt, "countries as an electricity-only storage solution without waste heat recovery; however, its ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 451.479pt, "potential in this configuration is more limited (Table 2). ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 482.435pt, "It is worthy emphasizing that PHPS systems that leverage waste heat emerges as a viable solution ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 501.39pt, "in solar-dominated countries when paired within the centralized configuration (i.e., operating as ")
  #line-at(85.091pt, 520.346pt, "a large, centralized CHP plant). Although, district heating and cooling systems are currently not ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 539.302pt, "widely deployed in such regions in Europe, some researchers suggest its potential in ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 558.257pt, "Mediterranean countries [48]. District heating is also present in Middle Eastern European ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 577.213pt, "countries, which have greater solar resource than northern countries, and could thus be suitable ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 596.169pt, "for integrating PHPS. While district heating in other countries like the United States is more ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 615.246pt, "prominent in northern regions, it is also present in southern states [49]. In these contexts, PHPS ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 634.202pt, "could contribute to the energy system in the centralized configuration. By combining with CTES, ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 653.157pt, "PHPS can generate waste heat to supply heating demand while providing the system with a LDES. ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 672.113pt, "This functionality complements the short-duration operation of Li-ion batteries, creating a more ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 691.069pt, "resilient and balanced energy system. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
