  #line-at(85.08pt, 66.955pt, "electricity is mainly supplied by solar and wind generation even though other renewable sources ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 86.032pt, "are expected in the future energy system. It is assumed that OCGT, whose use is limited by the ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 104.988pt, "5% of the CO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(150.36pt, 105.96pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(153.84pt, 105pt, " emissions constraints, represents other dispatchable power generators such as ")
  #line-at(85.061pt, 123.956pt, "biomass, hydropower, etc. The same occurs with energy storage, only PHPS and Li-ion batteries ")
  #line-at(85.061pt, 142.911pt, "are considered as electrical stores to balance wind and solar fluctuations. This study aims to ")
  #line-at(85.072pt, 161.867pt, "understand the use of PHPS in the energy system, the most critical parameters that may hinder its ")
  #line-at(85.072pt, 180.823pt, "prevalence, and the importance of the waste heat use for its feasibility. Thus, the assumed ")
  #line-at(85.072pt, 199.778pt, "simplified model allows answering these questions qualitatively. Further studies identifying the ")
  #line-at(85.072pt, 218.734pt, "energy storage characteristics that complement Li-ion batteries and PHS, and addressing current ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 237.811pt, "gaps of the energy system, have already been carried out by Gøtske et al. [36]. ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 268.767pt, "Space and time-resolution may also have an impact on the results. Each country simulation is ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 287.723pt, "represented by a single node; therefore, energy transmission from other countries is not ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 306.679pt, "considered. This limitation may impact on the PHPS’ feasibility, potentially leading to an ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 325.635pt, "oversized optimal capacity. This effect could be more significant in wind-dominated scenarios ")
  #line-at(85.083pt, 344.59pt, "where transmission lines are often used to manage variations in wind generation. The opposite ")
  #line-at(85.072pt, 363.546pt, "effect might occur given that renewable energy exports are also not considered in the simulations, ")
  #line-at(85.061pt, 382.502pt, "which is translated into larger energy curtailment. Additionally, bottlenecks within the national ")
  #line-at(85.05pt, 401.457pt, "transmission lines are neglected, resulting into lower optimal energy storage capacities. ")
  #line-at(85.05pt, 420.534pt, "Regarding time resolution, fast variations (<1 h) are not addressed as they fall out of the scope of ")
  #line-at(85.028pt, 439.49pt, "this study. Consequently, fast-demand response technologies, such as flywheels or ")
  #line-at(85.028pt, 458.446pt, "supercapacitors [8] are not analysed and do not compete with technologies under analysis. ")
  #line-at(85.017pt, 477.401pt, "Furthermore, relying on a single typical year neglects the inter-annual variability of solar and ")
  #line-at(85.028pt, 496.357pt, "wind generation, which could impact on the presented results [50]. ")
  #line-at(85.027pt, 527.313pt, "Our model represents the heating and electricity coupling but ignores potential synergies with the ")
  #line-at(85.016pt, 546.269pt, "industrial and transportation sectors. The industrial sector with high-temperature demand could ")
  #line-at(85.005pt, 565.225pt, "benefit from the heat stored in PHPS. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 599.28pt, "7.")
  #line-at(103.079pt, 599.28pt, "Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.08pt, 621pt, "This study has examined the role of PHPS systems in future renewable-dominated energy systems ")
  #line-at(85.08pt, 639.956pt, "by embedding them into stylized national models for wind- and solar-dominated countries. The ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 658.911pt, "results demonstrate that PHPS can play an important role in providing long-duration flexibility, ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 677.867pt, "particularly in settings where CTES is not available. In such contexts, PHPS emerges as a cost-")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 696.823pt, "effective option for balancing low-frequency renewable fluctuations thanks to its low cost per ")
  #line-at(85.069pt, 715.778pt, "energy capacity. ")
  #line-at(85.058pt, 746.735pt, "The analysis also highlights the decisive influence of waste heat utilization. When the low-")
  #line-at(85.058pt, 765.69pt, "temperature heat released during the power conversion process is recovered, PHPS becomes ")
]

